<title>INDIA: Yield at Indian 91-day t-bill falls to 8.86 pct.</title>
<headline>Yield at Indian 91-day t-bill falls to 8.86 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said it set a cut-off price of 97.84 rupees at its weekly 91-day treasury bills auction on Friday.</p>
<p>Money market dealers said the yield worked out to 8.86 percent, sharply down from 10.07 percent at the last auction.  </p>
<p>				  Bids received	Amount (Rs. million)</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Competitive			   37		     8,570.0</p>
<p>Non-competitive			1		     2,000.0</p>
<p>					  ---		    -------</p>
<p>Total				   38		    10,570.0</p>
<p>					  ---		    -------</p>
<p>				   Bids allotted     Amount (Rs. million)</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Competitive (1 partial)	    9		    4,108.90</p>
<p>Non-competitive (1 partial)	1			891.10</p>
<p>					  ---		    -------</p>
<p>Total				   10		     5,000.00</p>
<p>Devolvement : Reserve Bank of India			nil</p>
<p>		  Primary dealers				nil</p>
<p>Weighted average price - 97.88 rupees.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
